WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.560
Mannheim, 1933.

2
00:00:02.610 --> 00:00:05.350
A painting of a rabbi
is paraded in public,

3
00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:07.310
to be mocked and jeered.

4
00:00:07.360 --> 00:00:13.380
Four years later, in Munich, the Nazis hung
about 650 modern works in a show called

5
00:00:13.430 --> 00:00:14.980
Degenerate Art.

6
00:00:15.030 --> 00:00:17.850
The painter of that
rabbi was Marc Chagall:

7
00:00:17.900 --> 00:00:20.240
a modern artist, and a Jew.

8
00:00:20.290 --> 00:00:23.070
So how could a painting fight back?

9
00:00:23.120 --> 00:00:26.040
In this mission, you'll
decode four of his paintings,

10
00:00:26.090 --> 00:00:30.530
symbol by symbol, from a man at
prayer to a burning synagogue.

11
00:00:30.580 --> 00:00:33.150
Then you'll follow his
escape from wartime France,

12
00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:36.480
through Lisbon, to New York in 1941.

13
00:00:36.530 --> 00:00:40.050
Your mission: find out how
a painting could fight back.
